{"id": "EUVD-2026-93190", "enisaUuid": "97a6d8d6-c12b-3a56-b195-529baa232724", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nata: libahci: clear PxCLBU and PxFBU for AHCI_HFLAG_32BIT_ONLY\n\nA user reported that commit 105c42566a55 (\"ata: ahci: force 32-bit DMA for\nJMicron JMB582/JMB585\") made the JMicron JMB585 unusable on his board.\n\nThe failure is seen as soon as the ahci driver is probed, and booting with\niommu=off does not solve the problem.\n\nLooking at the AHCI specification, PxCLBU and PxFBU are both read only '0'\nfor HBAs that do not support 64-bit addressing.\n\nFor HBAs that do support 64-bit addressing, the registers are read write,\nwith a reset value that is Implementation Specific.\n\nWhen using the AHCI_HFLAG_32BIT_ONLY flag, the HBA does support 64-bit\naddressing, and a 32-bit DMA mask is set by simply clearing HOST_CAP_64.\nThus, in this case, we need to explicitly clear the registers to 0.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0191c9ff23ef1678dbfb5ad253a2dee92feb5d71", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f510f68208a1f673d7c7234a687be4671490e9c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4719424bb7cb9f20b73986bcb72dd528f0e5c6eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5a8b4737f68bbac8aa0685af0c8921e6003c22b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b28a17d4a9bb0aa38b48681c3927b012ba40eabe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b691a3e244278362e552439d6d3ee5a5d3703488", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7912ad8fb5233bb8cfe21d50df639c7f4854ff9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82e47533221d4746947b74d2e79a478c36c6433a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98262", "GHSA-599j-5783-gx62"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06063754-19a4-39c7-98a0-7e87266cea07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c7a42156d99bcea7f8173ba7a6034bbaa2ecb77c <b28a17d4a9bb0aa38b48681c3927b012ba40eabe"}, {"id": "0b213aeb-625e-3e51-9dda-09b11e875f28", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "0b739cc6-42d0-3861-a7f6-82e800cd24b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c7a42156d99bcea7f8173ba7a6034bbaa2ecb77c <b691a3e244278362e552439d6d3ee5a5d3703488"}, {"id": "3b9ceceb-abc0-3ba1-9ca8-91df6f85a6b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "487a2570-1fb0-3037-ab40-129c28407ec6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c7a42156d99bcea7f8173ba7a6034bbaa2ecb77c <82e47533221d4746947b74d2e79a478c36c6433a"}, {"id": "4cc70adb-f344-31b6-85e4-06219efd6614", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "4db120ac-332b-3e98-bb04-5edf390905b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "503f026e-656b-350d-b26b-598bae3aaffe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "643b84c4-22ef-3063-b12d-3c6748edf0f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "67b175fc-ba8e-3b1e-b234-55e397f6a88b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c7a42156d99bcea7f8173ba7a6034bbaa2ecb77c <4719424bb7cb9f20b73986bcb72dd528f0e5c6eb"}, {"id": "6c757257-75df-32fc-8c7a-19ac6004455e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.22"}, {"id": "840c4a25-00cc-32ac-bb76-299eae2d76f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c7a42156d99bcea7f8173ba7a6034bbaa2ecb77c <7912ad8fb5233bb8cfe21d50df639c7f4854ff9d"}, {"id": "92b074c1-b2d6-38bd-b8cf-7d7c7c98476a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c7a42156d99